    "narrative": "For the August 5th slate, Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into matchup exploitation against soft rotations. **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) and **Mickey Moniak** (75.75) anchor the lineup, benefiting from elite secondary indicators against Lowder and Martinez. **Soderstrom**\u2019s projection is bolstered significantly by his strong platoon split and favorable environment, while **Moniak** sees a massive 14% boost from both park factors and an advantageous SP matchup. **Seiya Suzuki** also warrants a high-leverage start (73.90), as he squares off against a vulnerable Lauer, allowing him to capitalize on his #2 spot in the order. Despite facing the formidable Mize, **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential play (68.61); his elite stolen base upside makes him start-worthy regardless of the matchup, even with the modest penalty for Mize\u2019s ability to hold runners.\n\nWe are navigating several constraints in the infield. **Austin Riley** (52.51) remains in the lineup despite a sub-optimal #8 spot, though he carries a 33% rain risk flag that requires monitoring. Conversely, **Cole Young** (37.96) was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine. While **Young**\u2019s profile offers upside, the optimizer penalized his score due to the unfavorable matchup against Anderson and the lack of a top-of-the-order buffer, ultimately keeping him below our 40.0 efficiency floor. **Brice Turang** (48.20) and **Gabriel Moreno** (54.60) occupy their respective slots as marginal starts; **Turang**\u2019s #1 lineup placement is the only factor keeping him viable against a high-tier arm like Skenes, while **Moreno** benefits from solid recency bias and a favorable projected batting position. We will keep a close watch on **James Wood**, who remains sidelined on the IL, limiting our depth as we aim to climb the standings in stolen bases.",
